%LC佐佐木
\dThis is actually my proper job, so don't worry about it.\nIf anything, I'm sorry about how things turned out earlier\ntoday.\d%K%P
「不，这才是我的职责。\n而且出门的时候还真是多有冒犯」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt is not your fault. The vice president is to blame\nhere.\d%K%P
「佐佐木先生没错。\n全都是副社长的错」%K%P
The board meeting we had after lunch was divided among the\nfive speakers with a 1:3:1:2:500 ratio time-wise.%K%P
午休结束之后开始的干部会议上，\n五个干部的发言比例是１：３：１：２：５００，\n这真是壮观的拷问啊。%K%P
And to tell the truth, the only person who said anything\nof significance was Chief Director Washizaki, the second\nspeaker.%K%P
顺带一提，有实际意义的发言，\n主要是比例占２的鷲崎董事做的。%K%P
Meanwhile, our managing director (speaking ratio: 1) just\nread my report aloud, and then later asked a few vague\namateur questions along the lines of how any of what was\nsaid actually connects to earning money.%K%P
我们泽嶋董事（发言比率为１），在我报告了之后，\n就偶尔说说『那，这样为什么盈利呢？』，\n就是这种直截了当的问题都问不出口的程度。%K%P
